course: dictionary
lesson: 11640
title: Arouse: to cause a feeling or wake someone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arouse is a verb, so it shows an action. Its forms are arouse, arouses, aroused and arousing. To arouse a feeling means to make that feeling start, like interest, curiosity, anger or suspicion. «The strange noise aroused her curiosity.» The noise made her want to find out more.
explain: Arouse can also mean to wake someone up, and this meaning is more old-fashioned, so you will meet it in stories. «The loud knock aroused the sleeping baby.» The knock woke the baby. Look at the clues: a sleeping baby and a knock show which meaning fits.
explain: Look at the words that come after arouse: suspicion, curiosity, interest, anger. These are feelings or thoughts that someone starts to have. Ask yourself: what started? If it is a feeling, arouse means to cause it.
fact: Arouse means to cause a feeling, such as interest, curiosity, anger or suspicion.
fact: «Arouse suspicion» means to make someone think something is wrong or not true.
fact: «Arouse curiosity» means to make someone want to find out more.
fact: In older stories, arouse can mean to wake someone up.
fact: Arouse is a verb, and its forms are arouse, arouses, aroused and arousing.
exercise: «The mysterious parcel aroused her curiosity.» What did the parcel do? | Made her throw it away | Made her laugh | *Made her want to find out more | Made her fall asleep
exercise: «His strange behaviour aroused suspicion among the teachers.» What does arouse suspicion mean? | Made the teachers forget his name | Made the teachers laugh loudly | *Made the teachers think something was wrong | Made the teachers feel very sleepy
exercise: Find the verb in «The bell aroused the sleeping cat.» Which word is the verb? | *aroused | bell | the | cat
test: «The loud crash aroused the old man from his nap.» What does aroused mean here? | Made him hungry | Made him sing | *Woke him up | Made him cross
test: «The new film aroused great interest in the town.» What did the film do to the town? | *Caused people to feel keen to know more | Made people feel bored | Made people go to sleep | Closed the cinema
exam: «Mia's rude joke aroused anger in her teacher.» What does aroused mean here? | Made the teacher laugh | Made the teacher hungry | Woke the teacher up | *Caused anger, so the teacher felt cross
